# Engine

The engine is plain Node. It must run in-process under Vitest and inside an Electron utility process. Do not import `electron` or React.

- Call `@cursor/sdk` only inside `CursorSdkRuntime`. The rest of the engine depends on `AgentRuntime`.
- Always `run.stream()` then `await run.wait()`. Dispose every agent in `finally`.
- A thrown `CursorSdkError` means the run never started. `result.status === "error"` means it started and failed.
- Pass `systemPrompt`, `tools`, `disallowedTools`, and `mcpServers` again on `Agent.resume()`. The SDK does not keep them.
- If `systemPrompt` is rejected, retry once with the instructions prefixed to the user prompt and surface a warning (decision D9).

```typescript
await using agent = await Agent.create({ /* local: { cwd } required */ });
try {
  const run = await agent.send(prompt);
  for await (const event of run.stream()) { /* map into our event type */ }
  return await run.wait();
} finally {
  /* await using disposes */
}
```
